# Bitter Baitling from Jang in Booty Bay for one Extravagant Extravaganza Coin,
# the prize for winning the Stranglethorn Fishing Extravaganza.
# Sources: npcs.json (Jang, Riggle Bassbait); quests.json (Master Angler 8193:
# 40 Speckled Tastyfish, repeatable, event 15); Forever's quest page for 8193
# (Arcanite Fishing Pole or Hook of the Master Angler, and the new spell
# "Master Angler!" 1299323, numbered beside Summon Bitter Baitling 1299341 in
# Forever's client data); items.json (Jang's stock; the Tastyfish keep 4
# hours).
# ASSUMED: Winning Master Angler gives the Extravagant Extravaganza Coin, and
# the first 50 players to hand in win, not only the first (a Forever fishing
# guide and a beta video; our data has no source for the coin). In-game check:
# hand in 40 Tastyfish to Riggle during the contest and look for the coin.
# ASSUMED: The contest runs on Sundays from 2 to 4 pm server time, with the
# Tastyfish schools along the coast, as in Classic (Riggle's quest text says
# "between 2pm and 4pm"; the weekday is Classic flow). In-game check: the
# first Sunday after launch.
# Master Angler is no quest you take: Riggle takes the 40 Tastyfish straight
# from his window and it never enters the log (the game's data has it as a
# quest handed in on the spot), so it is a `turnin direct` with a plain
# collect (#1699 sweep).

step Riggle Bassbait
  tip The Bitter Baitling costs one Extravagant Extravaganza Coin, the prize for winning the Stranglethorn Fishing Extravaganza. The contest runs on Sundays from 2 to 4 pm server time: be on the Booty Bay docks by Riggle Bassbait when it starts. Master Angler is not a quest you take: Riggle takes the fish straight from his window when you bring them. Bring your best Fishing skill and lures so no fish gets away, a mount and empty bags, and bind your hearthstone in Booty Bay.
  goto 27.4,76.9 "Riggle Bassbait"

step Schools of Tastyfish
  tip While the contest runs, schools of Speckled Tastyfish appear along the Stranglethorn coast, none inside Booty Bay. Fish 40 Speckled Tastyfish from them; each school lasts only a few casts, so ride on to the next as soon as one is gone. The arrow takes you up the west coast north of Booty Bay; more schools lie further north and just south of Booty Bay.
  loop
  goto 24.9,66.2
  goto 23.8,62.5
  goto 26.2,58.3
  goto 22.9,56.4
  goto 26.0,48.8
  goto 27.0,44.3
  collect 19807 x40                   -- Speckled Tastyfish

step Back to Riggle
  tip Hurry back and hand the 40 Tastyfish to Riggle: the first players to do so win, and the winners get the coin with their prize. If you are too late to win, Jang still pays a little gold for every 5 Tastyfish.
  turnin 8193 direct
  collect 274026 "Extravagant Extravaganza Coin" @27.4,76.9 -- The winner's coin, from Riggle

step Jang
  tip Jang, Riggle's apprentice, stands beside him on the Booty Bay docks and trades the Bitter Baitling for the coin.
  vendor 15078                        -- Jang
  buy 276275 "Bitter Baitling" npc 15078 -- 1 Extravagant Extravaganza Coin
